    "sensesNotes": "Darkvision 60 ft, Blindsight 30 ft (in water)",
    "tactics": "Deep Tides prioritize Engulf, targeting whoever the summoner indicates or whoever poses the greatest threat. On dry ground they are dangerous but limited; near water they become significantly more capable and will attempt to drag engulfed targets into any body of water present.",
    "attacksNotes": "<p>Slam [Combat]: Melee attack (Agil 6 + Melee Combat 3), Reach: 10 ft</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Margin 1:</strong>: 14 damage (7 + 7 Str)</li>\n<li><strong>Margin 2:</strong> 14 damage, DR halved (round up); target makes Fortitude save (1 success) or is knocked Prone</li>\n</ul>",
    "specialAbilitiesNotes": "<p>Engulf (Recharge 5-8) [Combat]: The Deep Tide surges over one creature of Medium size or smaller within 5 feet. Target makes a Reflex save (opposed by Agil 4 + Melee Combat 5). On failure, the creature is Grappled and Restrained within the elemental's body. Each round it remains engulfed, the creature takes 4 cold damage and must make a Fortitude [Easy] save or gain 1 Exhaustion level from the crushing water pressure. A creature can use an action to attempt to escape (Might or Athletics, [Hard] task). Water Mastery: While in water, the Deep Tide's ### Attacks ignore cover, and the Engulf recharge DC drops to 4-8.</p>",
